    "title": "Ariel Fifita joins Lobo Softball as assistant coach after standout Utah State career",
    "text": "Ariel Fifita has been appointed as an assistant coach for the University of New Mexico's Lobo Softball program, according to head coach Nicole Orgeron.\nFifita will take on responsibilities as a secondary hitting coach and will also work with the infielders.\nShe is a recent graduate of Utah State University, where she was recognized for her performance on the field. During her collegiate career, Fifita led the Aggies in several offensive categories including batting average, hits, doubles, total bases, and on-base percentage. She was named to the Second Team All-Mountain West in 2025 and also led her team in hits during her junior year. Over four seasons, she played in 175 games and made 168 starts as a shortstop.\nFifita earned a Bachelor of Science degree in psychology with a minor in sociology from Utah State University in 2025.",
